course: dictionary
lesson: 12881
title: Entangled: stuck and twisted up
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Entangled means caught and twisted up, so that you cannot move freely. «The kite got entangled in the tree branches.» The kite is stuck, and it cannot fly until someone frees it.
explain: Entangled can also mean a messy knot. «Her hair was entangled after the windy walk.» Hair twisted into a tangle is hard to brush out, just like a knot in string.
explain: Entangled can describe a difficult situation too. «The detective was entangled in a web of lies.» Nobody is tying the detective with rope. The word tells you the problem is hard to get out of.
explain: To check your meaning, swap in «stuck» or «twisted up» and read the sentence again. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Entangled means caught, twisted up, or hard to get free from.
fact: «Entangled» is an adjective, and it is also the past tense and past participle of the verb entangle.
fact: «A seal entangled in netting» means a seal is caught in a net and cannot swim freely.
fact: «Entangled wires» means wires twisted together in a messy knot.
fact: The word can describe real objects, like rope or hair, or a hard problem, like a lie or a tricky relationship.
exercise: «The fishing boat found a turtle entangled in a plastic net.» What does entangled mean here? | Painted bright blue | Swimming very fast | Sleeping on the sand | *Caught and twisted up so it cannot move freely
exercise: «My necklace is entangled with my hair.» What does entangled suggest? | Put away neatly in a box | Shiny and brand new | *Twisted together in a messy knot | Lost under the bed
exercise: «He was entangled in a difficult argument with his best friend.» Which word is closest in meaning? | Very quick | Far away | *Mixed up in a difficult problem | Happy and calm
test: Nadia says entangled means very happy. What does it really mean? | Floating on the water | Shiny and clean | *Caught and twisted up so it cannot move freely | Very happy and excited
test: Which sentence uses entangled to mean stuck in a difficult situation? | *«The spy was entangled in a web of lies.» | «The cat was entangled in a ball of wool.» | «The house was entangled and painted blue.»
exam: «Ella was entangled in her scarf, so she could not reach the door handle.» What does entangled show? | Ella was singing loudly | Ella was entering a race | Ella felt hot and sleepy | *Ella was caught in her scarf and could not move freely
